      say: `Next, plan against the fictional tenant, sending nothing. The named location is missing its IPv6 range, so it's an update. Ring 1's location policy already exists and matches. Three policies are new. And a policy someone made in the portal, covering every service principal, is reported but left alone. Then read the sign-ins. Ring 1 is clear and ready. In Ring 2, a deploy bot signed in from an address outside the egress ranges, so it would be blocked, and that ring isn't ready. Notice that no user sign-ins come back at all.`,
      detail: `Step 5, check the scope against the fictional tenant and plan, sending nothing: ./Invoke-NpiWorkloadCa.ps1 -Mode Plan -Cloud gcc -ScopePath tests/fixtures/ch08/scope.json -FixturePath tests/fixtures/ch08/tenant.json -OutputPath out/wca. Output: Checks: 0 Finding, 0 Warn, 2 Info. Plan: 3 Create, 1 NoChange, 1 NotInRepository, 1 Update. Dry run: 4 request(s) written to requests.json, none sent; rerun with -Apply to send them. location NL-WorkloadEgress Update; policy CA015-ServiceAccounts-LocationRestriction-Ring1 NoChange; policy CA037-WorkloadIdentities-HighRisk-Block-Ring1 Create; policy CA015-ServiceAccounts-LocationRestriction-Ring2 Create; policy CA037-WorkloadIdentities-HighRisk-Block-Ring2 Create; policy Workloads - block outside office (made in the portal) NotInRepository. The named location lacks the IPv6 range, so it is Update. Ring 1's CA015 already exists, report-only, and matches. The portal-made policy that targets ServicePrincipalsInMyTenant is reported and left alone. The two Info are Legacy Reports and Build Pipeline, eligible but not Tier 1. manifest.json lists fourteen GETs and no write. Step 6, read the service principal sign-ins and summarize them: ./Invoke-NpiWorkloadCa.ps1 -Mode SignIns -Cloud gcc -ScopePath tests/fixtures/ch08/scope.json -FixturePath tests/fixtures/ch08/tenant.json -From 2026-10-12 -To 2026-10-30T12:00:00 -OutputPath out/wca-signins. Output: Service principal sign-ins 2026-10-12T00:00:00Z to 2026-10-30T12:00:00Z (18 days): 6 read. Ring1: ready for enforcement: Mail Automation Clear, sign-ins 1; Payroll Export Clear, sign-ins 2. Ring2: not ready: Deploy Bot WouldBlock, sign-ins 2, outside the egress ranges: 203.0.113.7; HR Connector NoSignIns, sign-ins 0. Summary SHA-256: d7767949b75e1e5d3f6a6bef6501eb7de8e98ddd8a9f22e1eb82698969d8752e. The fixture's interactive user sign-in and its managed identity sign-in never come back: the filter asks for service principals only. Partner CRM's sign-in is counted as another service principal's, not judged. The hash is the same on every run with these inputs.`,
